Expire a sent command at its deadline even while the port stays readable.

Upstream waits pvt->timeout again once the deadline has passed, and only a
silent wait expires the command. With data= on PCUI, URCs such as ^RSSI or
^BOOT arriving more often than that keep a command without a reply waiting
forever.
Taken from the former phonelet URC port patch: only this check of its
monitor loop, without its second port. Applies after command-deadline.
License: GPL-2.0 (same as chan_dongle).
--- a/chan_dongle.c
+++ b/chan_dongle.c
@@ -522,6 +522,14 @@
 		}
 
 		t = at_queue_timeout(pvt);
+		ecmd = at_queue_head_cmd(pvt);
+		/* A sent command keeps its deadline even when the port stays readable.
+		 * Negative timeout also means no sent command, so inspect the head. */
+		if (ecmd && ecmd->length == 0 && t <= 0)
+		{
+			ast_log (LOG_ERROR, "[%s] timedout while waiting '%s' in response to '%s'\n", dev, at_res2str (ecmd->res), at_cmd2str (ecmd->cmd));
+			goto e_cleanup;
+		}
 		if(t < 0)
 			t = pvt->timeout;
 
